  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so all design choices carry maximum uncertainty. The first experiment must establish a performance floor to interpret all subsequent results. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest possible configuration: PCA is the most basic, well-understood RNA encoder with no learned parameters, singleprofile avoids the added complexity of aggregation, and no image modality is involved. This gives us (1) a clean baseline accuracy/F1 against which every other configuration can be compared, (2) a reference for whether multimodal fusion or more complex encoders actually add value, and (3) a fast, low-risk computation that won't waste budget on a complex setup before we know the system works end-to-end. Under a limited budget, anchoring the search with the simplest baseline maximizes the interpretive value of every future experiment."
}

